---
title: Material API
description: Reference for defineMaterial, resolveMaterial, and material types.
---

## Entrypoints

Adapter entrypoints export `defineMaterial`. Root and `/core` export both `defineMaterial` and `resolveMaterial`.

## `defineMaterial(input)`

```ts
interface FragMaterialInput {
	fragment: string;
	uniforms?: UniformMap;
	textures?: TextureDefinitionMap;
	defines?: MaterialDefines;
	includes?: MaterialIncludes;
	storageBuffers?: StorageBufferDefinitionMap;
}
```

Returns an immutable `FragMaterial` whose six fields are always present; omitted maps resolve to frozen empty objects. Nested uniform, texture, include, define, and storage-buffer descriptors are isolated from their inputs. Storage-buffer `initialData` reads return defensive typed-array copies, while caller-owned DOM and WebGPU objects remain unfrozen. The function validates the material fragment entrypoint, named identifiers, uniform values, defines, includes, storage buffers, and storage textures.

To change a declaration, call `defineMaterial(...)` with a new value and pass the replacement to `FragCanvas`. Do not mutate a returned material or one of its nested descriptors.

`fragment` must contain `fn frag(uv: vec2f) -> vec4f` in the main source. Material and pass colors use straight alpha until final canvas presentation.

Material helper functions can read the current fragment coordinates from `spektralFragment.uv`. Spektral initializes the fragment-local field before calling `frag(uv)`, so both values are equal at entry. See [Writing Shaders](/docs/writing-shaders) for the generated WGSL declaration and its scope.

## `resolveMaterial(material)`

Returns cached renderer input for a validated material:

- preprocessed `fragmentWgsl` and its line map;
- original fragment, include sources, define block, and captured source metadata;
- uniform values and sorted layout;
- texture definitions, sorted texture keys, and storage texture keys;
- sorted storage-buffer keys;
- deterministic material signature.

Use this low-level function for adapters, validation, or tooling. Applications normally pass the `FragMaterial` directly to `FragCanvas`.

Spektral-owned cache structures are deeply frozen: line-map entries, uniform layout entries and lookup tables, source metadata, and key lists cannot be mutated. Repeated calls for the same material return the same protected snapshot. Caller-owned `TextureSource` values retained as direct sources, including `data.source`, remain direct references and are not frozen. Copy an array before making local tooling edits.

See [Defining Materials](/docs/defining-materials) for the declaration/runtime boundary.
